10. Why do you use DB::transaction() when saving an employee and their projects together? What happens to a queued email sent inside a transaction that rolls back, and how do you prevent it?'
    We use DB::transaction because it provides us with concept of Atomocity i.e all queries either pass together or fail and the transaction rollback's back. In case of employee and projects we first update the empoyee data then sync and save their projects in the piviot table. So if the employee gets updated but the projects fail for some reason the incorrect data will reamin in the employees table. Does we have to wrap queries in the Database transaction so that the it is commited only when all queries are passing and if any fails the transaction can be rolled back preventing the inconsistent data.
    What happens to a queued email sent inside a transaction that rolls back, and how do you prevent it?=> the queued email sent inside the transaction remains as it is when it is called before commiting the transaction, which becomes inconsistent when the transaction is rolled back. Therefore it should be called after the Transaction commit is sucessful. does preventing inconsistent queued emails.

